{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1202548-how-much-blood-is-a-point-of-vitae","id":1202548,"title":"How much blood is a point of Vitae?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-03T06:57:03-07:00","id":1202548,"title":"How much blood is a point of Vitae?","content":"In milliters please.<br /> <br /> Also where do vampires store them? In their belly? Does their body work as some kind of Vitae tank?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T07:14:59-07:00","id":1202556,"title":"","content":"It's stored in their blood, or else you wouldn't be able to shed Vitae in the form of blood (containing DNA and other biological markers from all the victim's you've drank blood from). One Vitae is at most ca. 250 ml according to some old calculations done by my group (that I unfortunately can't back up). Above that and the vampire would have to contain more blood than is possible. Additionally, vampires of higher Blood Potency should in that case distil their Vitae into smaller amounts in order to be able to fit it inside their vascular system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T07:34:58-07:00","id":1202567,"title":"","content":"You could speak of how much Vitae is yielded from a particular volume of blood drained from a living human, but once it's consumed, Vitae resting within a Kindred system doesn't correspond to volumes of liquid. The body of an elder vampire with 75 Vitae isn't saturated with more fluid than a neonate storing 10, and a vampire exhausting a large amount of Vitae in a short amount of time doesn't physically become lighter or lose density. The blood sits fat and stagnant in a vampire's body, and it's plausible that a hungry vampire might be more sallow and less saturated than one well fed, but the blood isn't the Vitae, it's a vessel to carry it. Vitae isn't the blood. It's the life, an occult quality expressed in a physical medium.<br /> <br /> Where does the matter go and how is it conserved when an ancient monster drains an arena of victims dry to fill its gullet?<br /> <br /> &quot;Decent people shouldn't think too much about that.&quot; Academician Prokhor Zakharov, <i>For I Have Tasted the Fruit.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T07:38:54-07:00","id":1202570,"title":"","content":"Decent people? We're role-players!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T07:44:53-07:00","id":1202576,"title":"","content":"Average adult has 5 liters of blood. Average character has 7 health levels, translating to 7 points of blood. 5/7 = 714 mL<br /> <br /> Pretty sure that a vampire can move the Vitae in his body at will, so it could be anywhere. Though I suppose it first ends up in the stomach.<br /> <br /> My head canon has the Vitae spread out roughly equally, thickening in the parts of the body that are used. Vitae is what animates the undead after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2081,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","user":"Howalt","date":". 04-03-2018, 10:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T07:52:06-07:00","id":1202582,"title":"","content":"Consider that people can survive getting 7 lethal's worth of blood removed (although most people will require medical attention). They cannot survive complete exsanguination, meaning the Vitae taken represents less than the full 5 litres of blood the average adult contains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T07:57:34-07:00","id":1202587,"title":"","content":"Adding to the problem of vamps of higher BP storing massive amounts of vitae:<br /> <br /> I\u2019d say the vitae replaces matter (bones, marrow, dead flesh and mucus) that gets in the way. An elder is a litteral blood bag. As he spends vitae his bones hollow out, the marrow regrows in case structural integrity is compromised.<br /> <br /> Human body density is practically the same as water. So every kg corresponds to a volume of 1l. A 70k elder has more than enough space for 75 x .714 liters of vitae","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2081,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","user":"Howalt","date":". 04-03-2018, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T08:02:50-07:00","id":1202589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1202548-how-much-blood-is-a-point-of-vitae?p=1202582#post1202582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consider that people can survive getting 7 lethal's worth of blood removed (although most people will require medical attention). They cannot survive complete exsanguination, meaning the Vitae taken represents less than the full 5 litres of blood the average adult contains.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, theoretically. So, average character with 7 health levels is exsanguinated after 7 points of blood drained. Right? Theoretically the victim can be saved from turning all lethal into aggrevated, but a blood transfusion is a minimum requirement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2081,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","user":"Howalt","date":". 04-03-2018, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T09:26:28-07:00","id":1202623,"title":"","content":"Dr. Douglas Netchurch in the <b>Time of Thin Blood</b> book studies this very concept. Note that <i>vitae</i> -- that is, supernaturally transmuted blood -- varies widely per individual. Age and Generation play a large factor. Just because a Methuselah can store 50 points of vitae, that doesn't mean that they have five times the amount of physical blood inside them: it just means their body is more efficient at converting blood to vitae, and so there's more potency to be found in each liter of blood.<br /> <br /> So after careful study of the relative potency of vitae, Netchurch and Tremere researcher Maxius developed what they called the &quot;<a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Vitae_Efficacy_Unit\" target=\"_blank\">Vitae Efficiency Unit</a>&quot; -- basically they managed to identify the game mechanic of the Blood Point.<br /> <br /> Edit: Missed that this was VTR and not VTM. Basic concept still holds, though: there's no hard-and-fast rule for quantity of vitae, AFAIK.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":4,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","user":"IanWatson","date":". 04-04-2018, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T09:33:36-07:00","id":1202624,"title":"","content":"Vitae does not correlate to blood. Blood that isn't fresh provides less. Animal blood provides less. Different animals have different Vitae-to-Blood ratios, even. A human can be drained of all Vitae and still be alive. Elders store more vitae in the same space by making it more concentrated, not by physically holding more volume. Things with less concentrated Vitae-to-Blood ratios eventually become something of a drop in the bucket and difficult to extract the Vitae from. This is all in the book, with the possible exception of the storage thing. I can't remember where I read that, but it logically follows given that BP 10 vampires aren't all bloated balls of blood.<br /> <br /> Some quotes:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vitae is not blood; at least, not directly. Kindred create Vitae<br /> as a byproduct of processing the blood they absorb. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vitae is not blood. At least, not directly. Blood flows through<br /> mortal veins; Vitae through Kindred. However, when Kindred<br /> \u201cspend\u201d Vitae, their bodies do not lose the fluid that animates<br /> them; it simply becomes inert. Picture Kindred blood as paint.<br /> Blood is the oil, the water, the vessel. You can\u2019t paint with oil<br /> or water. <b>The Vitae is the pigment.</b> It brings color, it makes the<br /> paint vibrant. <b>It\u2019s only a small part of the mixture.</b> You could<br /> remove the pigment and still have a pail of fluid, it just wouldn\u2019t<br /> be very useful on a canvas. </div> </div> </div>In short, vampires store their Vitae in their blood. There is no fixed ratio. The analogy I've used before is a flavor packet, like Kool-Aid. A typical human might fit a teaspoon of it in a glass of water. A neonate might be able to store a tablespoon in a glass. A BP 10 Ancient is basically the entire flavor packet with just enough water to make a sugary sludge. To get a couple grains of powder from a squirrel requires drinking the entire cup, and anyone who's been drinking the Kool-Aid for more than a few days isn't going to get anything out of it; it isn't sweet enough to notice anymore.<br /> <br /> When you realize that &quot;Vitae&quot; literally means &quot;Life,&quot; it becomes more clear why healthier humans have more of it, bigger animals have more of it, and why blood loses it quickly once it is removed from a living vessel. It's also why it's more of a flavor or &quot;pigment&quot; in the blood that has to be processed and filtered out of it than some actual physical component. It's impossible to give a ratio, because every living thing you encounter has different amounts of &quot;life&quot; energy in it, even if they have roughly the same amount of blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T09:38:42-07:00","id":1202627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Howalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1202548-how-much-blood-is-a-point-of-vitae?p=1202589#post1202589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, theoretically. So, average character with 7 health levels is exsanguinated after 7 points of blood drained. Right? Theoretically the victim can be saved from turning all lethal into aggrevated, but a blood transfusion is a minimum requirement.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You are not exsanguinated after seven points of Vitae drained. You would be dead if that is the case, but instead you are dying and can be saved with first aid. You can run out of Vitae before you lose too much blood to survive, and usually will run out before death. In fact, given that you cause damage per Vitae drained, and there is no provision for continued damage after there is no more Vitae to take, it seems fairly clearly (if counter-intuitively) stated that it's the removal of Vitae that causes the damage, not the draining of blood, and (it seems, based on this information)that relatively little blood is actually taken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T16:11:54-07:00","id":1202784,"title":"","content":"Gotta love the haughty tone that\u2019s so prevalent on these forums<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1202548-how-much-blood-is-a-point-of-vitae?p=1202624#post1202624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When you realize that &quot;Vitae&quot; literally means &quot;Life,&quot; .</div> </div> </div> </div>I am familiar with dr. Pangloss and the dormitive principle.<br /> <br /> Vitae -has- to be correlated to blood, even if it is only that blood serves as a substrate to vitae. Like you say yourself: that\u2019s where a vampire stores it. In fact, as a human loses blood he loses vitae. And to imbibe vitae a vampire needs to drink blood. What is more, vitae expenditure requires blood be shed, this is most clear when it comes to such practices as ghouling and cruac.<br /> <br /> That different species have different vitae to blood ratio\u2019s doesn\u2019t in the slightest mean that the ratio of vitae to blood in a particular species cannot be determined, if only by approximation.<br /> <br /> I always assumed that vampires not being able to exsanguinate people per RAW was an artefact of the combination of vampire feeding rules and gmc damage rules for mortals. It seems counter topical for a vampire not being able to feed until the heart gives out. But sure, I suppose I should go by raw:<br /> <br /> Class 4 hemorrhaging has a person go into hypovolemic shock after losing about 40% of their blood, i.e. 2 liters. This seems a good correlate for right most health box marked as lethal, there is still a (slight) chance of saving the victim.<br /> <br /> 2/7 = 285 mL of blood (which is probably how Tessie\u2019s group arrived at their number) as an average volume of blood, carrying 1 point of vitae.<br /> <br /> With this new volume it is entirely possible for even a vampire who suffers from dwarfism to hold 100 points of Vitae. <br /> <br /> Considering the bulk of a human body consists of water, it is thematically appropriate to suppose that the bulk of a vampire\u2019s consists of blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2081,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","user":"Howalt","date":". 04-03-2018, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T16:17:31-07:00","id":1202787,"title":"","content":"You might look into physics where blood is only our world's extension or anchor to it but the power itself extends elsewhere, only really applicable by the vampire hosts.<br /> <br /> We know, for instance, that vampires are not blood bags. They're increasingly desiccated corpses. They don't seem to have blood unless it's manufactured via Blush of Life.<br /> <br /> It would certainly be easy to just say a pint of blood is a health and a corresponding pint of Vitae but that falls apart after a bit. When you drain someone down to 1 Health, for instance, they would be running on a pint of blood, which doesn't seem like it would be accurately depicted by wound penalties and instead require immediate health care (which is generally needed after Aggravated damage takes place).<br /> <br /> Plus we know Vitae isn't blood on its own, it's life taken from blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-03-2018, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T16:55:30-07:00","id":1202804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1202548-how-much-blood-is-a-point-of-vitae?p=1202787#post1202787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We know, for instance, that vampires are not blood bags. They're increasingly desiccated corpses. They don't seem to have blood unless it's manufactured via Blush of Life.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d say the \u2018fact\u2019 of torpid vampires shrivveling up to parchment mummies only supports the idea that, yes, vampires are bloodbags in the same way that humans are waterbags. Once the vampire has been woken and fed, his healthy looking, undead features return. Or would you say that it requires the blush for an elder not to look desiccated? It might require the blush to infuse the stale blood in a vampire\u2019s veins with a semblance of life, but when you expend vitae, for example to ghoul someone, that vitae is certainly carried in blood, even if that blood is the dead-tissue mixture of all your past victims, gooey and yuck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T17:05:09-07:00","id":1202807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Howalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1202548-how-much-blood-is-a-point-of-vitae?p=1202804#post1202804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d say the \u2018fact\u2019 of torpid vampires shrivveling up to parchment mummies only supports the idea that, yes, vampires are bloodbags in the same way that humans are waterbags. Once the vampire has been woken and fed, his healthy looking, undead features return. Or would you say that it requires the blush for an elder not to look desiccated? It might require the blush to infuse the stale blood in a vampire\u2019s veins with a semblance of life, but when you expend vitae, for example to ghoul someone, that vitae is certainly carried in blood, even if that blood is the dead-tissue mixture of all your past victims, gooey and yuck.</div> </div> </div> </div>They appear dead when they go into Daysleep, whether they have 1, 10 or 75 Vitae. And if you cut them, they do not bleed, unless Blush of Life is involved, though that 1 Vitae to 'wake up' at night seems to cover most of their animation, Humanity covers the rest, with low Humanity vampires looking increasingly dead or inhuman.<br /> <br /> And you can expend 1 Vitae in the form of a single drop of Vitae. There's no blood involved except as the original source of it. You only have blood come out if you've activated Blush of Life to make you fit in with other living beings.<br /> <br /> This is detailed in the About Vitae section. Also throughout first edition in things like the Blood book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-03-2018, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T17:17:04-07:00","id":1202809,"title":"","content":"Meanwhile, the Strix are snickering at vampires for thinking Vitae to be bound in blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T17:19:00-07:00","id":1202810,"title":"","content":"Also, you can be in Torpor with full Vitae. And yes, the lower the Humanity a vampire has, the more corpse-like they appear, so an Elder will have problems without Blush of Life.<br /> <br /> More quotes:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When one of the Kindred falls to torpor, she appears dead.<br /> Her skin tightens over her flesh and dries out. Her joints<br /> harden, and the top layer of her tissue turns to a faint, ashen<br /> dust. [...] As well, a vampire can voluntarily fall into torpor, to shake<br /> off the feeding limitations imposed by her Blood Potency. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Monstrous (Humanity 2): A monstrous vampire is barely<br /> recognizable as human, unless he\u2019s specifically acting the part<br /> and using the blush of life. He looks like a moving corpse, with<br /> dry flesh tightened over bones and a faint red hue to his eyes. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Animalistic (Humanity 1): [...] While she could fake humanity with a<br /> bit of blood, she can\u2019t be bothered, and instead looks like a corpse,<br /> a statue, a morbid doll. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T17:28:35-07:00","id":1202816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1202548-how-much-blood-is-a-point-of-vitae?p=1202809#post1202809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile, the Strix are snickering at vampires for thinking Vitae to be bound in blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, it's something other vampires have figured out. Among the various proto-vampires you have some who can make Vitae from emotions, memories, and one's lifespan. Even among the more well-known Kindred we have breath-drinkers and liver-eaters.<br /> <br /> 'Vampires know perfectly well that it isn\u2019t the organic components of blood that sustain them. Blood is a lot more than liquid flesh: blood is the material vehicle for a supernatural life-force.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T18:43:35-07:00","id":1202837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1202548-how-much-blood-is-a-point-of-vitae#post1202548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In milliters please.<br /> <br /> Also where do vampires store them? In their belly? Does their body work as some kind of Vitae tank?</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://media.giphy.com/media/srTYyZ1BjBtGU/giphy.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Howalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1202548-how-much-blood-is-a-point-of-vitae?p=1202784#post1202784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gotta love the haughty tone that\u2019s so prevalent on these forums</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">And that's not appropriate. Respect other people and respect the conversation.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-03-2018, 09:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T18:52:12-07:00","id":1202841,"title":"","content":"From the Blood, p49:<br /> <br /> 'The moment blood is swallowed it is immediately transformed into Vitae. It does not sit in the vampire\u2019s stomach, but is instead absorbed into all parts of the corpus with similar ease: bone, muscle, sinew and other tissues. This occurs automatically, with no effort on the part of the Kindred. Even a vampire lying in bloodless torpor for a century will respond this way if fed a supply of blood.'<br /> <br /> This is the section that gets into the differences between blood and Vitae, the latters' 'instincts' in that it can coil back into its owner and away from most harm, and its need to feeding the Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-03-2018, 09:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T20:10:33-07:00","id":1202854,"title":"","content":"All right, for the record: I do not deny that that Vitae =|= blood. All I\u2019ve tried to approach is an answer to the question: how many ml would Vitae take up, when it\u2019s extracted in the form of (human) blood.<br /> <br /> Low humanity vampires have nothing to do with it.<br /> <br /> Vampires in torpor with vitae in their system do not address the point made.<br /> <br /> Vampires looking death like without the blush is an open door, the question was about shrivveling up.<br /> <br /> That (other kinds of) vampires may extract Vitae in different manners doesn\u2019t matter.<br /> <br /> The Blood description may be seen as evidence of the process as I\u2019ve argued for it (vamps being blood bags)<br /> <br /> The only point I see reason to concede is that Vitae may be contained in lesser, more concentrated volumes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T22:54:26-07:00","id":1202879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Howalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1202548-how-much-blood-is-a-point-of-vitae?p=1202854#post1202854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All right, for the record: I do not deny that that Vitae =|= blood. All I\u2019ve tried to approach is an answer to the question: how many ml would Vitae take up, when it\u2019s extracted in the form of (human) blood.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">The only point I see reason to concede is that Vitae may be contained in lesser, more concentrated volumes.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Then the question you are asking is not &quot;What volume of blood does a point of Vitae take up?&quot;</span><br /> <br /> The thing you are asking is <i>what volume of blood a vampire needs to drain to distill a point of Vitae</i>, which is an inherently variable question due to how feeding limitations manifest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T00:40:22-07:00","id":1202895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1202548-how-much-blood-is-a-point-of-vitae?p=1202787#post1202787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might look into physics where blood is only our world's extension or anchor to it but the power itself extends elsewhere, only really applicable by the vampire hosts.<br /> <br /> We know, for instance, that vampires are not blood bags. They're increasingly desiccated corpses. They don't seem to have blood unless it's manufactured via Blush of Life.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What makes you think vampires don't carry blood in their corpse-like bodies? There are literally countless of examples in the core rule book talking about the blood inside a vampire's body.<br /> <br /> Read page 98 the 'Daysleep and Waking' part, the 'About Vitae' part for example.<br /> <br /> So no, we don't know vampires aren't blood bags at all, in fact we know the opposite is true. Vampires are blood bags. They do carry blood in their bodies just like mortals do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 04-04-2018, 03:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T00:48:48-07:00","id":1202897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1202548-how-much-blood-is-a-point-of-vitae?p=1202895#post1202895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What makes you think vampires don't carry blood in their corpse-like bodies? There are literally countless of examples in the core rule book talking about the blood inside a vampire's body.<br /> <br /> Read page 98 the 'Daysleep and Waking' part, the 'About Vitae' part for example.<br /> <br /> So no, we don't know vampires aren't blood bags at all, in fact we know the opposite is true. Vampires are blood bags. They do carry blood in their bodies just like mortals do.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue as I see it is whether the \u2018volume\u2019 of Vitae corresponds one-to-one with volume of blood, not whether vampires have blood in their bodies in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T00:58:33-07:00","id":1202899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1202548-how-much-blood-is-a-point-of-vitae?p=1202897#post1202897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The issue as I see it is whether the \u2018volume\u2019 of Vitae corresponds one-to-one with volume of blood, not whether vampires have blood in their bodies in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, in that case, I'll just say here what I wanted to edit into my previous post:<br /> <br /> I'd say the ratio of vitae to blood varies on a lot of factors and I don't think it's ever an exact number or ratio. A large cow will only give you 3 or so Vitae, even if you drain it dry it won't give you more than that. Yet even a petite (size 4) human gives you 5 Vitae at the very least, assuming you drain her all the way until she drops into a coma or dies. Yet an elder vampire of normal human size can hold 75 vitae. Yet it also states that when a vampire uses Vitae, he doesn't lose blood, the blood merely loses Vitae. Not to mention when a vampire goes in torpor to lower his Blood Potency, one speaks of &quot;thinning the blood&quot;, meaning the amount of vitae the vampire's blood can hold becomes less, even though the vampire in torpor doesn't literally lose or leak blood.<br /> <br /> So in short: it varies and there is no single correct answer to the OP's question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T05:13:39-07:00","id":1202953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1202548-how-much-blood-is-a-point-of-vitae?p=1202895#post1202895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What makes you think vampires don't carry blood in their corpse-like bodies? There are literally countless of examples in the core rule book talking about the blood inside a vampire's body.<br /> <br /> Read page 98 the 'Daysleep and Waking' part, the 'About Vitae' part for example.<br /> <br /> So no, we don't know vampires aren't blood bags at all, in fact we know the opposite is true. Vampires are blood bags. They do carry blood in their bodies just like mortals do.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue with this is that, presumably to avoid using the term Vitae over and over, they sometimes call it blood, this is actually mentioned. The Blood, again, p48, 'Moments after a vampire ingests blood, the \ufb02uid is transformed into Vitae and remains so as long as it remains within the vampire\u2019s body. There is a precise distinction between the two substances, both in the game mechanics and from the perspective of most Kindred, despite how often they might use the words blood and Vitae interchangeably.'<br /> <br /> But once blood is ingested by a vampire, it becomes Vitae, there is no human or animal blood in them, it's just Vitae, and it's suffused throughout their entire body, like it said, from kidney to toenails to femur to forehead.<br /> <br /> In-game, if you wanted to make measurements, you would weigh a victim before and after a feeding, and weigh a vampire before and after theirs. I'm guessing this isn't in many of the books, but if it might be in one of the clan books or Night Slayers, from hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-04-2018, 08:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T11:02:07-07:00","id":1203069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1202548-how-much-blood-is-a-point-of-vitae?p=1202837#post1202837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"https://media.giphy.com/media/srTYyZ1BjBtGU/giphy.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\">And that's not appropriate. Respect other people and respect the conversation.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Bait? I'm serious, and look we started a fun discussion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T12:04:43-07:00","id":1203090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1202548-how-much-blood-is-a-point-of-vitae?p=1202953#post1202953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The issue with this is that, presumably to avoid using the term Vitae over and over, they sometimes call it blood, this is actually mentioned. The Blood, again, p48, 'Moments after a vampire ingests blood, the \ufb02uid is transformed into Vitae and remains so as long as it remains within the vampire\u2019s body. There is a precise distinction between the two substances, both in the game mechanics and from the perspective of most Kindred, despite how often they might use the words blood and Vitae interchangeably.'<br /> <br /> But once blood is ingested by a vampire, it becomes Vitae, there is no human or animal blood in them, it's just Vitae, and it's suffused throughout their entire body, like it said, from kidney to toenails to femur to forehead.<br /> <br /> In-game, if you wanted to make measurements, you would weigh a victim before and after a feeding, and weigh a vampire before and after theirs. I'm guessing this isn't in many of the books, but if it might be in one of the clan books or Night Slayers, from hunter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But the examples I gave pretty clearly talk about blood as in, the red sticky stuff. For example, when the book says a vampire doesn't bleed when you cut him because the Beast holds the <b>fluid</b> inside the vampire's body, it says the Vitae pulls the <b>blood</b> back into the vampires body. It also says that when a vampire uses blush of life, it <b>bleeds normally, but doesn't lose Vitae</b>. It even talks about what blood from a vampire looks like and how it's darker than human blood.<br /> <br /> Under the Daysleep section it talks about how waking is like a reverse heart attack and how the heart starts pumping again when the vampire wakes up. Pumping for what? Why would a vampire's heart pump if it didn't contain liquid, e.g. blood? Logically it wouldn't even be able to pump at all if it didn't contain any liquid.<br /> <br /> Then of course there is Kindred Senses on page 90 and 91, which talks about tasting and tracking blood, and it says that Kindred blood is like a mixture of all of the victims he drank from.<br /> <br /> <br /> Vitae =/= blood, I get that. but the idea that vampire bodies don't contain blood seems weird and unfounded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 04-04-2018, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T12:59:24-07:00","id":1203109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1202548-how-much-blood-is-a-point-of-vitae?p=1203090#post1203090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the examples I gave pretty clearly talk about blood as in, the red sticky stuff. For example, when the book says a vampire doesn't bleed when you cut him because the Beast holds the <b>fluid</b> inside the vampire's body, it says the Vitae pulls the <b>blood</b> back into the vampires body. It also says that when a vampire uses blush of life, it <b>bleeds normally, but doesn't lose Vitae</b>. It even talks about what blood from a vampire looks like and how it's darker than human blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since all blood ingested turns into Vitae, it's pretty clear that this blood mentioned is Vitae. There is no actual blood inside a vampire except when using Blush of Life, when they bleed with supernaturally manufactured blood to keep up their cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T13:10:12-07:00","id":1203110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1202548-how-much-blood-is-a-point-of-vitae?p=1203109#post1203109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since all blood ingested turns into Vitae, it's pretty clear that this blood mentioned is Vitae. <b>There is no actual blood inside a vampire except when using Blush of Life</b>, when they bleed with supernaturally manufactured blood to keep up their cover.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which I find an unfounded claim for which I can find no source to back that up. Can you?<br /> <br /> You make an awful lot of assumptions here which goes against a lot of the written material. Again, lets bring up the part under Kindred Senses on page 91:<br /> <br /> A vampire can smell the presence of blood from about ten yards<br /> or meters per dot of Blood Potency without rolling. Multiply this<br /> range by her Auspex dots. If she\u2019s tasted a particular human\u2019s blood,<br /> she can add her Blood Potency to any rolls to track him by scent.<br /> <b>Kindred blood does not offer this advantage, since it\u2019s mostly old,<br /> dead, and its smell is a blend of all the vampire\u2019s recent victims.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> That sentence is clearly talking about actual blood, not Vitae.<br /> <br /> Again, I'd also like to bring up this sentence, again:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Vampires do not naturally bleed when cut. <u>The Vitae is<br /> possessive; it pulls the blood back to the body</u> in the way a<br /> drop of mercury absorbs back into a pool.</b><br /> <br /> That sentence makes it very very clear that vampires most definitely have liquid blood in their bodies. It even mentions how Vitae interacts with that blood. Yes, Vitae and blood are two separate things in a vampire's body, but the vampire clearly has both. To say a vampire doesn't have blood in his body seems, again, unfounded. But feel free to prove me wrong by quoting a part of the book that specifically states vampires do not have blood in their bodies.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> I'd also like to add; if vampires don't have liquid blood, then how in the world do BP6+ vampires drink from other vampires? Last time I checked, vampires don't have breath drinking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 04-04-2018, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T13:34:11-07:00","id":1203117,"title":"","content":"Well, since vampires don\u2019t normally breathe in the first place, it\u2019d be kind of stupid to think breath drinking works normally on them. But the answer to that is, the same way a vampire under BP 6 drinks vitae from another vampire. They grapple their target, extend their fangs and bite the other vampire and proceed to suck out their vitae. Or it could work without the grappling on a more voluntary basis. One of my characters filled a Solo cup or shot glass with 4-6 vitae of her own and handed it over to her grandsire, who\u2019s blood potency rating was 8, to drink.<br /> <br /> <br /> And by the way, you might want to try reading that same section where you yanked out how vitae holds onto blood. It verifies nofather\u2019s assertions that ingested blood isn\u2019t pooled into a central reservoir to be squirted out later on demand, it\u2019s suffused through the kindred\u2019s body (which resets every day) or manufactured when the blush of life is activated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 04-04-2018, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T14:22:29-07:00","id":1203136,"title":"","content":"I feel I should post one of my earlier quotes again, but with different emphasis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Vitae is not blood.</b> At least, not directly. Blood flows through<br /> mortal veins; Vitae through Kindred. However, <b>when Kindred<br /> \u201cspend\u201d Vitae, their bodies do not lose the fluid that animates<br /> them; it simply becomes inert.</b> Picture Kindred blood as paint.<br /> Blood is the oil, the water, the vessel. You can\u2019t paint with oil<br /> or water. <b>The Vitae is the pigment.</b> It brings color, it makes the<br /> paint vibrant.<b> It\u2019s only a small part of the mixture.</b> <b>You could<br /> remove the pigment and still have a pail of fluid, </b>it just wouldn\u2019t<br /> be very useful on a canvas. </div> </div> </div>Vampires, by the book, have both blood and Vitae, and spending Vitae does not get rid of the blood that holds it.<br /> <br /> I feel like people are holding positions that are extremes when the reality is in the middle. Vampires are not bereft of blood, but they also aren't storing the blood they drink. They have their own blood, which is animated and imbued with Vitae filtered out from the blood they drink, and which remains even if that Vitae is spent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T16:11:21-07:00","id":1203169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1202548-how-much-blood-is-a-point-of-vitae?p=1203110#post1203110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which I find an unfounded claim for which I can find no source to back that up. Can you?</div> </div> </div> </div>I literally quoted the source twice.<br /> <br /> The Blood p48, 'Moments after a vampire ingests blood, the \ufb02uid is transformed into Vitae and remains so as long as it remains within the vampire\u2019s body. <br /> <br /> The Blood p49, 'The moment blood is swallowed it is immediately transformed into Vitae. It does not sit in the vampire\u2019s stomach, but is instead absorbed into all parts of the corpus with similar ease: bone, muscle, sinew and other tissues. This occurs automatically, with no effort on the part of the Kindred. Even a vampire lying in bloodless torpor for a century will respond this way if fed a supply of blood.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You make an awful lot of assumptions here which goes against a lot of the written material. Again, lets bring up the part under Kindred Senses on page 91:<br /> <br /> A vampire can smell the presence of blood from about ten yards<br /> or meters per dot of Blood Potency without rolling. Multiply this<br /> range by her Auspex dots. If she\u2019s tasted a particular human\u2019s blood,<br /> she can add her Blood Potency to any rolls to track him by scent.<br /> <b>Kindred blood does not offer this advantage, since it\u2019s mostly old,<br /> dead, and its smell is a blend of all the vampire\u2019s recent victims.</b><br /> <br /> That sentence is clearly talking about actual blood, not Vitae. </div> </div> </div>Why would it be talking about corpses that don't bleed and not the Vitae they throw around to drug people?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, I'd also like to bring up this sentence, again:<br /> <br /> <b>Vampires do not naturally bleed when cut. <u>The Vitae is<br /> possessive; it pulls the blood back to the body</u> in the way a<br /> drop of mercury absorbs back into a pool.</b><br /> <br /> That sentence makes it very very clear that vampires most definitely have liquid blood in their bodies. It even mentions how Vitae interacts with that blood. Yes, Vitae and blood are two separate things in a vampire's body, but the vampire clearly has both. To say a vampire doesn't have blood in his body seems, again, unfounded. But feel free to prove me wrong by quoting a part of the book that specifically states vampires do not have blood in their bodies. </div> </div> </div>As I said, and quoted, they use the terms Vitae and blood interchangeably. Did you notice that your two points, if correct, contradict each other? If Vitae pulls 'regular' blood back into the body, how are they leaving things to be smelled with Kindred senses?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Edit:</b> I'd also like to add; if vampires don't have liquid blood, then how in the world do BP6+ vampires drink from other vampires? </div> </div> </div>They take Vitae and whatever remnants of Life they have from them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Last time I checked, vampires don't have breath drinking. </div> </div> </div>Check again. It's in Mythologies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T16:29:26-07:00","id":1203171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1202548-how-much-blood-is-a-point-of-vitae?p=1203117#post1203117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, since vampires don\u2019t normally breathe in the first place, it\u2019d be kind of stupid to think breath drinking works normally on them. But the answer to that is, the same way a vampire under BP 6 drinks vitae from another vampire. They grapple their target, extend their fangs and bite the other vampire and proceed to suck out their vitae. Or it could work without the grappling on a more voluntary basis. One of my characters filled a Solo cup or shot glass with 4-6 vitae of her own and handed it over to her grandsire, who\u2019s blood potency rating was 8, to drink.<br /> <br /> <br /> And by the way, you might want to try reading that same section where you yanked out how vitae holds onto blood. It verifies nofather\u2019s assertions that ingested blood isn\u2019t pooled into a central reservoir to be squirted out later on demand, it\u2019s suffused through the kindred\u2019s body (which resets every day) or manufactured when the blush of life is activated.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think you're missing the point. But I want to elaborate on your post anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>&quot;proceed to suck out their vitae.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> How? What would be the vessel to carry the vitae from one vampire to the other? I know the answer, but I'd like to see you answer this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>&quot;And by the way, you might want to try reading that same section where you yanked out how vitae holds onto blood. It verifies nofather\u2019s assertions that ingested blood isn\u2019t pooled into a central reservoir to be squirted out later on demand&quot;</b><br /> <br /> That does not prove nofather's point at all. It merely proves that vitae =/= blood, something I already agreed upon. It proves that the blood of a vampire's victim is absorbed into the entire body of the vampire rather than just sitting in his stomach or being stored somewhere, which is something I also agreed upon. What this does not prove is that vampires don't have blood in their bodies at all. That's wrong. They do have blood in their bodies, their own blood. I've proven that on multiple occasions, with multiple examples from the book.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> I'm gonna tag <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> in here cause this post basically functions as a solid answer to your last post as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 04-04-2018, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T16:30:56-07:00","id":1203173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1202548-how-much-blood-is-a-point-of-vitae?p=1203136#post1203136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like people are holding positions that are extremes when the reality is in the middle. Vampires are not bereft of blood, but they also aren't storing the blood they drink. They have their own blood, which is animated and imbued with Vitae filtered out from the blood they drink, and which remains even if that Vitae is spent.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly the point I was trying to make. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T16:31:52-07:00","id":1203174,"title":"","content":"Once again, poetic &amp; common language leaves many an argument. They say Blood Is Life, so of course the vampires refer to Vitae as simply blood, especially when their main medium of interacting with Vitae is blood. Except that it\u2019s not.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I see that Maina pretty much settled the argument already. Now let\u2019s see how long it takes till someone else brings up this issue again, since it seems to crop up every now and then. Honestly, it feels like a leftover from Masquerade where we literally had Blood Points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 04-04-2018, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T17:02:08-07:00","id":1203185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1202548-how-much-blood-is-a-point-of-vitae?p=1203169#post1203169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Check again. It's in Mythologies.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was specifically one of the things that changed in the switch to 2e \u2014 Kindred breath-drinking is a thing you get from Strix possession now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T20:11:35-07:00","id":1203263,"title":"","content":"To be fair, Breath drinking is possible with Protean 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T20:40:03-07:00","id":1203272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1202548-how-much-blood-is-a-point-of-vitae?p=1203263#post1203263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, Breath drinking is possible with Protean 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but that's\u2026 that's <i>very </i>different from what most folks would think of as &quot;breath-drinking.&quot; That's you <i>turning into fog and entering somebody's lungs</i> in a state where you can also drain life from open wounds within the bounds of your gaseous form at the apex of an uncommon Discipline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T04:43:13-07:00","id":1203367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1202548-how-much-blood-is-a-point-of-vitae?p=1203272#post1203272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, but that's\u2026 that's <i>very </i>different from what most folks would think of as &quot;breath-drinking.&quot; That's you <i>turning into fog and entering somebody's lungs</i> in a state where you can also drain life from open wounds within the bounds of your gaseous form at the apex of an uncommon Discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes it's not really what you think about when you think about breath drinking but i thought it was still a thing to point out when you took up the strix ability. Protean 5 is quite scary and quite closely connected to the strix it seems. Breath drinking, becoming smoke, flashes of yellow, like the gleaming of eyes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T13:40:04-07:00","id":1203507,"title":"","content":"Speaking of which, what happens if a vampire feeds on the Vitae of a mortal who has been completely drained via Breath Drinking? There's blood but no Vitae so... No nourishment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T13:52:27-07:00","id":1203512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1202548-how-much-blood-is-a-point-of-vitae?p=1203507#post1203507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of which, what happens if a vampire feeds on the Vitae of a mortal who has been completely drained via Breath Drinking? There's blood but no Vitae so... No nourishment?</div> </div> </div> </div>Breath drinking causes damage too. The big benefit of it is you don't have to be obvious about it at higher levels, and can sit on a crowded train and slowly drain the life out of people without having to bite them.<br /> <br /> It's all in the <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/12201/Mythologies?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">Mythologies</a> book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}